Package: ADMIT
Title: ADMixture-mapping Inclusion Threshold
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ganze", "Yu", email = "ganzeyu@unc.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Chooses the global-ancestry window for an admixture-mapping cohort from the
    local-ancestry caller's own error rate, instead of by convention. An individual raises the
    scan's non-centrality parameter only when their call is more reliable than about half the
    pooled reliability, and where that leaves the threshold is set by the background false-call
    rate: what the caller reports in people who carry none of the focal ancestry, which can be
    measured directly in any cohort. The package estimates that rate, returns the detection- and
    estimation-optimal cuts with the efficiency cost of any other cut, and reports how many
    unadmixed individuals each cut admits. Reliability curves measured against held-out-founder
    truth are supplied and can be rescaled to another caller; a caller the package has not seen can
    be calibrated from scratch.
